From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@thingino.com>
Date: Tue, 08 Sep 2026 00:00:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ingenic-sdk: t41/gc5603 publish min_fps/max_fps to video_in

Second T40-copy fallout in t41/sensor-src/gc5603.c (see 0004 for the
clock-name one). T40's struct tx_isp_video_in has no min_fps/max_fps
members, so the T40 original never set them; T41's does
(isp/t41/include/tx-isp-common.h:643-644) and the T41 ISP firmware
*requires* them. gc5603.c is the only T41 gc5603 variant that was never
updated: t41/gc5613.c:751-752, t41zrt/gc5603.c:774-775 and 1019-1020 and
t41/gc5603s0.c:1105-1106 all set both fields, gc5603.c sets neither, so
they stay 0 from the zeroed struct tx_isp_sensor.

Consequence, traced in libt41-firmware.a 1.2.6
(tisp_ae_sensor_par_ctrls_update, .text+0x21634):

  +0x354  lhu  v0, 0x3a(tisp_par_info + idx*160)   ; max_fps numerator
          bnez v0, ok
          isp_printf(..., "max fps error !!!", 647)
          sw   0x00190001 -> core+0x67c            ; fall back to 25/1
  +0x3a8  lhu  v0, 0x36(tisp_par_info + idx*160)   ; min_fps numerator
          bnez v0, ok
          isp_printf(..., "min fps error !!!", 652)
          sw   0x00050001 -> core+0x680            ; fall back to 5/1

so both warnings fire together purely because the numerators are zero -
not because a requested rate is out of range. Worse, the tail of the
same function (+0x46c..+0x4a0) then unconditionally overwrites both
words with ((val << 1) & 0xffff0000) + 2 recomputed from the SAME zero
fields, clobbering the 25/1 and 5/1 fallbacks with 0/2 - i.e. the AE
runs with max_fps = min_fps = 0 for the life of the stream.

Fix mirrors t41zrt/gc5603.c: set both in sensor_set_attr() (so mode and
WDR switches keep them current) and once more at the end of
sensor_attr_check() (so they are valid before the first attr sync).

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@thingino.com>
---
--- a/4.4.94/sensor-src/t41/gc5603.c
+++ b/4.4.94/sensor-src/t41/gc5603.c
@@ -816,6 +816,8 @@
 	sensor->video.mbus.field = TISP_FIELD_NONE;
 	sensor->video.mbus.colorspace = wsize->colorspace;
 	sensor->video.fps = wsize->fps;
+	sensor->video.max_fps = wsize->fps;
+	sensor->video.min_fps = SENSOR_OUTPUT_MIN_FPS << 16 | 1;

 	return 0;
 }
@@ -1080,6 +1082,8 @@

 	sensor_set_attr(sd, wsize);
 	sensor->priv = wsize;
+	sensor->video.max_fps = wsize->fps;
+	sensor->video.min_fps = SENSOR_OUTPUT_MIN_FPS << 16 | 1;

 	return 0;

